/// known-gap: interp has no block overlay syntax (overlay name ... xx); the interpreter is being retired
/// An overlay's `every 1 tick` block that brings a host to its erase
/// condition erases it before anything acts that tick: it doesn't act,
/// and nobody picks it.
<>G |
    name: ""
    hp: 2
    decision other
        targets: G
    xx
    judge
        other: yell(self, other >> target)
    xx
    transition erase where @hp <= 0
xx
overlay bleeding
    every 1 tick => @hp |= @hp - 2
xx
act yell(g, t)
    a | g >> name
    b | t >> name
    say("{a} yells at {b}")
xx
p <> G | name: "p", hp: 2
q <> G | name: "q", hp: 9
r <> G | name: "r", hp: 9
:overlay!(p, bleeding)
tick()
say(:len(:objects(it >> name == "p")))
